{"version": 2, "width": 80, "height": 24, "timestamp": 1767142386, "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/bash", "TERM": "xterm-256color"}, "title": "Structured Error Handler / serr - Tuulbelt"}
[0.00418, "o", "# Structured Error Handler Demo\r\n"]
[1.005956, "o", "\r\n# 1. Show demo with JSON output (default)\r\n"]
[1.507525, "o", "$ serr demo\r\n"]
[2.559154, "o", "{\r\n  \"name\": \"StructuredError\",\r\n  \"message\": \"Failed to connect to database\",\r\n  \"context\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"operation\": \"handleGetUser\",\r\n      \"component\": \"UserController\",\r\n      \"metadata\": {\r\n        \"endpoint\": \"/api/users/12345\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"timestamp\": \"2025-12-31T00:53:08.789Z\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"operation\": \"fetchUserProfile\",\r\n      \"component\": \"UserService\",\r\n      \"metadata\": {\r\n"]
[2.559411, "o", "        \"userId\": \"12345\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"timestamp\": \"2025-12-31T00:53:08.786Z\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"operation\": \"connectToDatabase\",\r\n      \"component\": \"DatabaseClient\",\r\n      \"metadata\": {\r\n        \"host\": \"localhost\",\r\n        \"port\": 5432\r\n      },\r\n      \"timestamp\": \"2025-12-31T00:53:08.786Z\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n"]
[4.57828, "o", "\r\n# 2. Show demo with human-readable text format\r\n"]
[5.079591, "o", "$ serr demo --format text\r\n"]
[6.087978, "o", "[DB_CONNECTION_FAILED] Failed to connect to database\r\n\r\nContext:\r\n  → handleGetUser (UserController) {\"endpoint\":\"/api/users/12345\"}\r\n  → fetchUserProfile (UserService) {\"userId\":\"12345\"}\r\n  → connectToDatabase (DatabaseClient) {\"host\":\"localhost\",\"port\":5432}\r\n\r\nCaused by:\r\n  Connection refused\r\n"]
[8.106856, "o", "\r\n# 3. Parse a JSON error\r\n"]
[8.608244, "o", "$ serr parse '{\"message\":\"Test error\",\"code\":\"TEST_CODE\",\"context\":[]}'\r\n"]
[9.628288, "o", "[TEST_CODE] Test error\r\n"]
[11.648111, "o", "\r\n# 4. Validate JSON error format\r\n"]
[12.149582, "o", "$ serr validate '{\"message\":\"Hello\"}'\r\n"]
[13.161118, "o", "Valid error format\r\n"]
[14.180791, "o", "\r\n# 5. Show help\r\n"]
[14.682161, "o", "$ serr --help\r\n"]
[15.699269, "o", "Structured Error Handler - Error format with context preservation\r\n\r\nUsage:\r\n  structured-error-handler <command> [options] [input]\r\n\r\nCommands:\r\n  parse <json>     Parse a JSON error and format it\r\n  validate <json>  Validate JSON error format\r\n  demo             Show a demo of structured errors\r\n\r\nOptions:\r\n  -f, --format <format>  Output format: json, text (default: json)\r\n  -s, --stack           Include stack traces in output\r\n  -h, --help            Show this help message\r\n\r\nExamples:\r\n  # Parse and format an error\r\n  structured-error-handler parse '{\"message\":\"test\",\"context\":[]}'\r\n\r\n  # Validate error format\r\n  structured-error-handler validate '{\"message\":\"test\"}'\r\n\r\n  # Show demo\r\n  structured-error-handler demo --format text\r\n"]
[17.719259, "o", "\r\n# Done! Handle structured errors with the serr command.\r\n"]
